firmware: qcom: scm: allow qseecom on the Arduino UNO Q

The UNO Q (arduino,imola, QRB2210) has the QSEECOM interface, version
0x1402000, but qcom_scm skips it: "qseecom: untested machine, skipping".
The firmware of the board keeps what is written to its EFI variables at
runtime in RAM only (the RTStorageVolatile variable names
VolatileVars.bin), so a variable such as RTCInfo is gone after the next
reset. The uefisecapp client of the interface is the way to keep one.

Add the board to the allowlist so the client can bind.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2288,6 +2288,7 @@
  + any potential issues with this, only allow validated machines for now.
  */
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
+	{ .compatible = "arduino,imola" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
